eli: heads up 1 opened a tiny troubleshooting blurb for streaming responses cut by mid-stream 429s. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4999. want feedback on minimal snippet and UX warnings.
zoe: +1 for a tiny snippet. recommend: detect 429, short backoff, retry once, then trim oldest turns and resume. mention cache invalidation header.
frank: agree. also add a one-line warning that trimming may change outputs and to run a small smoke eval.
eli: draft snippet (keeps pseudo-code small):
```
// pseudo: detect 429 mid-stream, retry then trim+resume
resp, err := client.Stream(ctx, prompt)
if api.IsRateLimit(err) {
  sleep(200ms)
  resp2, err2 := client.Stream(ctx, prompt)
  if api.IsRateLimit(err2) {
    trimmed := TrimOldTurns(prompt, 2)
    resumed := helpers.ResumeWithTrim(ctx, client, trimmed, prompt.Meta)
    if resumed.Headers.Get("x-prefix-invalidate") == "1" {
      cache.Clear(prompt.PrefixID)
    }
    return Stitch(resumed, /*original*/ prompt)
  }
  return resp2
}
return resp
```
zoe: looks good. i'll add a short caption: "Trimming can alter outputs; validate with your eval set."
